**New evidence**
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Party chief gives directions at teleconference between Government, localities","publisher":"Nhan Dan Online","publication_date":"2022-01-05","url":"https://en.nhandan.vn/party-chief-gives-directions-at-teleconference-between-government-localities-post109323.html","claim":"Nguyen Phu Trong gave directions to implement the 2022 socio-economic development scheme and praised the 2021 rebound as the basis for further recovery.","locator":"article lead / opening paragraphs","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous state-media report of Trọng's own directions at a national economic coordination meeting.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 ruler-period evidence.","ruler_attribution":"Direct to Trọng; it shows his framing of economic priorities and coordination role.","contrary_evidence":["This is agenda-setting rather than proof of implementation.","The piece is state media and emphasizes the leadership line."],"lenses":["5B.1","5B.7","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Major targets of socio-economic development plan in 2022","publisher":"Government News (VGP / baochinhphu.vn)","publication_date":"2022-01-28","url":"https://en.baochinhphu.vn/major-targets-of-socio-economic-development-plan-in-2022-111220128100722544.htm","claim":"The 2022 socio-economic plan set targets of roughly 6-6.5 percent GDP growth, about 4 percent CPI inflation, and about 5.5 percent labor-productivity growth, with a 67 percent trained-worker target.","locator":"resolution table / Appendix 1","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary government plan with explicit numeric targets for the target year.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 policy baseline.","ruler_attribution":"Structural party-state policy baseline under Trọng's leadership; not a personal speech act.","contrary_evidence":["Targets are intentions, not outcomes.","The resolution does not by itself show implementation quality."],"lenses":["5B.1","5B.3","5B.6","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Vietnam: 2022 Article IV Consultation-Press Release; Staff Report, and Statement by the Executive Director for Vietnam","publisher":"International Monetary Fund","publication_date":"2022-07-05","url":"https://www.imf.org/en/publications/cr/issues/2022/07/05/vietnam-2022-article-iv-consultation-press-release-staff-report-and-statement-by-the-520395","claim":"The IMF said Vietnam had robust growth and sound fundamentals, with prudent policies producing prolonged high growth, price stability, low public debt ratios, and strong FDI and trade flows that boosted external buffers.","locator":"summary / report description","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary IMF country report summarizing macroeconomic fundamentals and policy context.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Covers the 2022 economy directly.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect to Trọng through the party-state macro framework; not a direct order transcript.","contrary_evidence":["It evaluates the economy as a system, not Trọng's personal management.","It also notes the need for continued reforms and agile policymaking."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.4","5B.6","5B.7","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"IMF Staff Completes 2022 Article IV Mission to Vietnam","publisher":"International Monetary Fund","publication_date":"2022-04-21","url":"https://www.imf.org/en/news/articles/2022/04/21/pr22127-vietnam-imf-staff-completes-2022-article-iv-mission-to-vietnam","claim":"The IMF said policy support and vaccination rollout would help Vietnam achieve 6.0 percent growth in 2022 and that inflation was expected to edge up to 3.9 percent by end-2022 while remaining below the 4 percent target.","locator":"press-release bullet and follow-on paragraph","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous IMF mission statement with explicit growth and inflation forecasts.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 evidence.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect to Trọng through the government's macro policy setting.","contrary_evidence":["This is a forecast, not an ex post outcome.","The statement stresses downside risks and uneven recovery."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Effective Policy Implementation is Crucial for Vietnam to Reach High-Income Status by 2045, World Bank Group Report Says","publisher":"World Bank","publication_date":"2022-05-18","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/news/press-release/2022/05/18/effective-policy-implementation-is-crucial-for-vietnam-to-reach-high-income-status-by-2045-world-bank-group-report-says","claim":"The World Bank said Vietnam must shift its growth model and sharply improve government capacity to coordinate and implement economic policy reforms and public investments, with stronger transparency and accountability.","locator":"lead paragraph and report summary","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary World Bank press release summarizing a country diagnostic focused on institutions and implementation.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 structural-policy context.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but substantial; this describes the institutional capacity under Trọng's party-state.","contrary_evidence":["This is a recommendation, not proof that reforms were implemented.","It focuses on institutions more than household outcomes."],"lenses":["5B.6","5B.7","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Taking Stock: Vietnam Economic Growth Update, August 2022","publisher":"World Bank","publication_date":"2022-08-08","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/country/vietnam/publication/taking-stock-vietnam-economic-growth-update-august-2022","claim":"The World Bank reported a strong rebound in the first half of 2022, projected 7.5 percent GDP growth for 2022, and expected inflation to remain about 4 percent, while noting that tertiary education was underperforming.","locator":"Part I lines 43-45 and Part II lines 51-52","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary World Bank country update with clear macro and productivity claims for the target year.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 evidence.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect to Trọng through the broader policy environment; the report does not isolate personal decisions.","contrary_evidence":["The report emphasizes structural weaknesses in higher education and skills.","The growth forecast is not the same as realized welfare gains."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.6","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Addressing Chronic Poverty, Ensuring Sustainable Economic Mobility Keys to Achieving Vietnam’s High-income Aspirations","publisher":"World Bank","publication_date":"2022-04-28","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/news/press-release/2022/04/28/addressing-chronic-poverty-ensuring-sustainable-economic-mobility-keys-to-achieving-vietnam-s-high-income-aspirations","claim":"The World Bank said poverty fell from 16.8 percent to 5 percent over 2010-2020, but inequality increased marginally, COVID-19 set poverty reduction back, and many households remained economically vulnerable.","locator":"main release text lines 143-151","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary World Bank poverty and equity press release with concrete distributional findings.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Baseline and 2022 policy context.","ruler_attribution":"Contextual rather than directly attributable to Trọng; it defines the household distribution problem he inherited.","contrary_evidence":["This is mostly about 2010-2020 rather than a 2022 choice.","It does not isolate Trọng's direct role in earlier poverty gains."],"lenses":["5B.8","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Launching of Taking Stock Report - “Education to Grow”: Speech by Carolyn Turk, Country Director for the World Bank in Vietnam","publisher":"World Bank","publication_date":"2022-08-08","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/news/speech/2022/08/08/launching-of-taking-stock-report-education-to-grow-speech-by-carolyn-turk-country-director-for-the-world-bank-in-vietnam","claim":"The World Bank said Vietnam needed a skilled workforce to become a knowledge-driven, productivity-driven economy, but tertiary enrollment remained low and firms reported difficulty finding technical, managerial, and leadership skills.","locator":"speech lines 45-52","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary World Bank speech summarizing a report on human capital and productivity constraints.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 evidence.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect to Trọng through the education and productivity policy environment.","contrary_evidence":["The speech explicitly praises general education performance, so the picture is mixed.","This is an external assessment, not a ruler action record."],"lenses":["5B.6","5B.7","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Consumer price index, gold and USD price indexes, December 2022","publisher":"General Statistics Office of Vietnam","publication_date":"2022-12-29","url":"https://www.nso.gov.vn/en/data-and-statistics/2022/12/consumer-price-index-gold-and-usd-price-indexes-december-2022/","claim":"Vietnam's CPI rose 3.15 percent in 2022, meeting the National Assembly target, and the GSO said the government had directed ministries and localities to stabilize prices and limit inflation's negative impact.","locator":"2022 CPI section / year-end explanation","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary national statistics release with explicit annual inflation outcome and policy response.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 outcome.","ruler_attribution":"Structural party-state management rather than a Trọng-only decision.","contrary_evidence":["Inflation data do not prove overall economic stewardship.","The note also shows fuel prices were a major inflation driver."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Socio-economic situation in the fourth quarter and 2022","publisher":"General Statistics Office of Vietnam","publication_date":"2023-01","url":"https://www.nso.gov.vn/en/data-and-statistics/2023/01/socio-economic-situation-in-the-fourth-quarter-and-2022/","claim":"The GSO reported 2022 realized state-budget investment of 511.6 trillion VND, equal to 85.2 percent of plan, and foreign direct investment realized in Vietnam at nearly 22.4 billion USD, up 13.5 percent year on year.","locator":"development investment section","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary official year-end statistical release with implementation and outcome figures.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 implementation and outcome data.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect to Trọng; these are state performance outcomes under his leadership.","contrary_evidence":["Public investment execution was still short of plan, so this is not unqualified success.","The page is a statistical summary, not a causal attribution study."],"lenses":["5B.6","5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Report on foreign direct investment in 2022","publisher":"Ministry of Planning and Investment","publication_date":"2022-12-26","url":"https://mpi.gov.vn/en/Pages/2022/Report-on-foreign-direct-investment-in-2022-403479.aspx","claim":"As of December 20, 2022, Vietnam had attracted about 27.72 billion USD in newly registered, adjusted, and contributed FDI capital, while realized FDI capital was estimated at 22.4 billion USD, up 13.5 percent year on year.","locator":"FDI inflows of Vietnam section","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary ministry report with explicit year-end FDI performance figures.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 implementation and inflow data.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect to Trọng through the national investment climate and policy framework.","contrary_evidence":["Strong inflows do not prove equal distribution or high-quality jobs.","The report is promotional and should be read alongside independent assessments."],"lenses":["5B.4","5B.6","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Party chief chairs anti-corruption meeting","publisher":"Government News (VGP / baochinhphu.vn)","publication_date":"2022-08-17","url":"https://en.baochinhphu.vn/party-chief-chairs-anti-corruption-meeting-111220817162948058.htm","claim":"Trọng urged stronger anti-corruption mechanisms, tighter control of assets and incomes, review of bidding, auction, financial management, land use, and public property rules, and faster handling of corruption cases.","locator":"article body lines 166-171","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary government report of a dated Trọng-led anti-corruption meeting with specific reform directions.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 ruler-period evidence.","ruler_attribution":"Direct to Trọng; this is one of his core governing domains.","contrary_evidence":["Anti-corruption crackdowns can also freeze legitimate transactions and chill investment.","The article reports intent and case-processing orders, not measured effectiveness."],"lenses":["5B.5","5B.7"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Sixth plenum of 13th Party Central Committee opens in Ha Noi","publisher":"Government News (VGP / baochinhphu.vn)","publication_date":"2022-10-03","url":"https://en.baochinhphu.vn/sixth-plenum-of-13th-party-central-committee-opens-11122100310563027.htm","claim":"At the sixth plenum, Trọng presided over deliberations on 2022 socio-economic performance, the 2023 development and budget plans, and modernization and industrialization through 2030 and 2045; the article also reported GDP growth of 8.83 percent for January-September 2022.","locator":"article body lines 165-174","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary government report of a dated plenum where Trọng set the agenda for economic review and planning.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 ruler-period evidence.","ruler_attribution":"Direct to Trọng in his role as Party General Secretary and agenda setter.","contrary_evidence":["This is a review/planning setting, not proof of execution quality.","The growth figure is a period snapshot, not a full-year result."],"lenses":["5B.1","5B.7","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Vietnam gathering momentum for sustainable development: Party leader","publisher":"VietnamPlus","publication_date":"2022-12-31","url":"https://en.vietnamplus.vn/vietnam-gathering-momentum-for-sustainable-development-party-leader/246404.vnp","claim":"In his year-end interview, Trọng said Vietnam's 2022 achievements helped its 2023 growth outlook and that the country had achieved and surpassed 14 of 15 targets, with GDP growth around 8 percent.","locator":"search result snippet / opening paragraph","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"State media interview with a dated quote and explicit year-end performance summary.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 ruler-period evidence.","ruler_attribution":"Direct to Trọng; it is his own retrospective assessment of 2022 performance.","contrary_evidence":["This is self-evaluation and likely emphasizes the favorable side.","The article does not break out distribution or household-level losses."],"lenses":["5B.1","5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Vietnam fires top stock market regulator over \"wrongdoing\"","publisher":"Reuters via MarketScreener","publication_date":"2022-05-20","url":"https://www.marketscreener.com/news/latest/Vietnam-fires-top-stock-market-regulator-over-wrongdoing-40483702/","claim":"Reuters reported that Vietnam's anti-corruption drive had caused a $40 billion wipeout for stocks and rattled investor confidence after high-profile corporate arrests tied to market manipulation.","locator":"lines 937-940","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous Reuters reporting, but accessed through a republisher and focused on market effects.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 evidence.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect to Trọng through the anti-graft campaign he led.","contrary_evidence":["The article is about market damage from enforcement, not proof that enforcement was unjustified.","Investor confidence effects do not prove the underlying arrests were baseless."],"lenses":["5B.5","5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Analysis: Vietnam's anti-graft crackdown chills supply chains, investment","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-11-28","url":"https://m.investing.com/news/commodities-news/analysis-vietnams-antigraft-crackdown-chills-supply-chains-investment-2952525?ampMode=1","claim":"Reuters reported that the anti-corruption drive had paralysed many routine transactions, caused shortages of drugs and petrol, and dampened investor confidence by making officials reluctant to greenlight procurement and investment.","locator":"opening paragraphs / article summary","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous Reuters analysis with concrete economic-distortion claims, though accessed via a republisher.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 evidence.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect to Trọng through the campaign's system-wide effects.","contrary_evidence":["This is analysis, so causation is partly interpretive.","The article highlights problems created by enforcement intensity, not necessarily corruption itself."],"lenses":["5B.5","5B.6","5B.9","5B.10"]}

**Search and rejection summary**
- I screened roughly 30 documents across IMF, World Bank, Vietnam government portals, VietnamPlus, Nhan Dan, GSO, MPI, and Reuters-republished reporting.
- I retained 15 non-duplicative URLs because they collectively cover macro stability, growth, FDI, public investment, inflation, poverty, education, anti-corruption, and the main downside effects of the crackdown.
- I rejected duplicate mirrors of the same Reuters items, older 2018 anti-corruption explainers, and post-2022 follow-ups that did not add materially new evidence for the 2022 target year.
- I also set aside some pages that were blocked or timed out on open; where the search-result snippet already carried the relevant claim, I used that instead of forcing a weaker substitute.
- I did not use the client matrix.

**Remaining gaps**
- Public evidence on 5B.2 is thin: I found formal authority and policy steering, but not strong 2022 evidence that Trọng personally appointed or empowered particular economic professionals.
- Household-level welfare and regional distribution are only partially visible through poverty, inequality, and education indicators; direct 2022 ruler attribution there is mostly indirect.
- The record supports a mixed chapter: strong macro recovery and continued state investment coexist with weak public-investment execution, low tertiary attainment, persistent vulnerability, and a graft drive that appears to have chilled parts of the economy.
- More search would help mainly on appointment decisions, implementation of the recovery package, and any direct evidence that Trọng personally corrected or worsened specific economic mistakes.
